 "remarks": "Welcome to \"Nor Tor,\" one of Greenwich's most distinguished English manor estates, privately nestled on 3.44 acres in the heart of town. An extraordinary residence where architectural heritage, timeless craftsmanship, and modern luxury converge atop beautifully appointed grounds. Meticulously preserved and thoughtfully enhanced through a comprehensive three-year restoration led by renowned architect Ira Grandberg, this magnificent manor encompasses four exceptional levels of living space. The front-to-back entrance hall, enveloped in bespoke Gracie wallcoverings, establishes an immediate tone of refined elegance for the rooms beyond. In one direction, the English oak library offers a richly intimate retreat, while the other leads to a grand living room defined by its sophisticated proportions. This space flows effortlessly into a sun-drenched lounge with three exposures, where French doors offer a seamless transition to the gardens and the pool. At the heart of the home, a gourmet center-island kitchen and breakfast room serve as a vibrant hub, connecting gracefully to a well-appointed butler's pantry and the beautifully adorned formal dining room. Beyond the main entertaining spaces, a private office, media center, wine cellar, and dedicated rooms for exercise and leisure provide an exceptional collection of spaces tailored for both quiet productivity and grand-scale celebration. The private quarters set above it all are equally distinguished.",
